{"conclusion": "n_9db13a904e", "createdAt": "2026-10-25T23:31:06Z", "id": "arg_9b1f0c9db6", "op": "assert", "premises": ["n_5a52d00ac7", "n_80e62f4f2a", "n_c7a1c55511", "n_d990aee664"], "provenance": [{"file": "Knowledge Wiki/wiki/Java Static Initializer Block.md", "message": "setup box for static variables — runs automatically when the JVM loads the class", "session": "backfill-fix-2026-10-26"}], "statement": "Static initialisation that needs .put() or .add() action statements cannot live in the open class body, since the class body admits only declarations, so Java needs a static {} block for complex static initialisation."}
{"createdAt": "2026-10-26T00:15:19Z", "id": "arg_1b3ad47091", "op": "retract", "reason": "Inherits overstatement about Adam as sign descent"}
